+### Explanation of changes
+
+**`src/_pytest/python.py`** — In `Module._importtestmodule`, the `CollectError` raised when a `skip.Exception` is caught outside of a test no longer tells users to use `pytestmark = pytest.mark.{skip,skipif}` (which does not stop the module from being executed/imported and therefore fails when the module contains syntax not understood by the running interpreter). The new message explains that calling `pytest.skip` at module level will skip the entire module, and directs users to `allow_module_level=True` when that is their intention, otherwise to the `pytest.mark.skip`/`pytest.mark.skipif` decorators for individual tests/classes.
+
+**`testing/test_skipping.py`** — Updated `test_module_level_skip_error` to assert on the new message wording. The existing `test_module_level_skip_with_allow_module_level` continues to verify that `allow_module_level=True` works (and is now the behavior explicitly documented by the error message).
+
+### Running the relevant tests
+
+You can run the affected tests with:
+
+```
+python -m pytest testing/test_skipping.py::test_module_level_skip_error testing/test_skipping.py::test_module_level_skip_with_allow_module_level testing/test_skipping.py::test_invalid_skip_keyword_parameter -v
+```
+
+Both `test_module_level_skip_error` and `test_module_level_skip_with_allow_module_level` should pass with the updated message.
+
+### Note on the second idea (`skip_module` API)
+
+I deliberately did **not** introduce a new `skip_module` public API. `pytest.skip(msg, allow_module_level=True)` already provides exactly that capability; the real problem was that the error message hid this from users. Introducing a redundant public API would expand the public surface without clear benefit, and the maintainers' preferred direction here is to guide users to the existing, documented `allow_module_level` flag. If you do want an explicit `skip_module` helper as well, let me know and I can add it (plus its own tests and documentation), but I'd recommend against it for the reasons above.
+
+### Documentation
+
+I could not update the docs directly because the relevant `.rst` files (e.g. `doc/en/reference/reference.rst` which documents `pytest.skip`, and the how-to guides) were not provided in the chat. The `skip` docstring in `src/_pytest/outcomes.py` already documents `allow_module_level`, so no code-level docstring change is strictly required. If you'd like me to also improve the user-facing docs, please add the specific documentation files to the chat and I'll update them.
